# ─── Frontend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave EMPTY for local development: Vite proxies /api, /socket.io and /uploads
# to the backend, so everything is same-origin and the session cookie works.
#
# Set it ONLY for a split deployment (e.g. Vercel frontend + tunnelled backend).
# No trailing slash. The app switches to bearer-token auth automatically.
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-tunnel.ngrok-free.app

# ─── Voice / video calls ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WebRTC needs a TURN relay whenever the two ends can't reach each other
# directly — symmetric NAT, mobile carriers, most office networks. Without one
# the call negotiates and then silently never connects.
#
# Left unset, the app falls back to Open Relay's free public TURN, which is fine
# for testing but shared and rate-limited. Point these at your own for anything
# real (Twilio, Cloudflare Calls, Metered, or a self-hosted coturn).
# VITE_TURN_URL=turn:your-turn-host:3478,turns:your-turn-host:5349?transport=tcp
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
